  "result": "Perfect! All 82 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Created `src/numbering.js`** with `nextInvoiceNumber(existingNumbers, issueDate)`:\n- Generates invoice numbers in format `INV-<year>-<counter>`\n- Counter is 4 digits, zero-padded (0001\u20139999)\n- Counter resets each year based on the year in issueDate\n- Finds the maximum counter for the given year from existing numbers\n- Returns `ok('INV-YYYY-NNNN')` or `fail('DATE_INVALID')` for bad dates\n- Returns `fail('AMOUNT_INVALID')` if counter would exceed 9999 or existingNumbers is not an array\n- Ignores malformed existing numbers gracefully\n\n**Added `issueInvoice(invoice, existingNumbers)` to `src/invoices.js`**:\n- Validates invoice status is `'draft'` (returns `fail('NOT_DRAFT')` otherwise)\n- Calls `nextInvoiceNumber()` to generate a number\n- Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with `number` set and `status: 'issued'`\n- Never mutates the input invoice\n- Preserves all other invoice properties (customerId, issueDate, lines)\n\n**Added tests:**\n- 12 tests in `test/numbering.test.js` covering:\n  - First invoice of a year (0001)\n  - Sequential numbering\n  - Multi-year handling with counter reset\n  - Padding with zeros\n  - Large counters and overflow\n  - Date validation\n  - Handling malformed existing numbers\n  \n- 7 tests in `test/invoices.test.js` covering:\n  - Number assignment and status change\n  - Next number calculation\n  - Year-based counter reset\n  - Error conditions\n  - No mutation of original invoice\n  - Preservation of properties\n\nAll 82 tests pass \u2705",
